=begin
  high_type - Highlighting types with universal link coloring.  Download HTSORTER for highlights while looking in bags.

  Item type-specific highlighting using GameObj data with universal link coloring functionality.
  Replaces linktothefast with comprehensive link color management and type-specific overrides.
  Shared configuration with other scripts via UserVars.
  Frontend-aware: XML preset tags on Wrayth/Stormfront, GSL highlight codes on Wizard/Avalon.
  Per-frontend config: commands edit the XML or GSL side matching the active frontend.

  Examples:
    ;high_type                     - Show current configuration
    ;high_type quiet               - Load silently with item count
    ;high_type reset               - Reset configuration to defaults
    ;high_type add gem thought     - Add or update type color assignment
    ;high_type colors              - Show color examples with actual formatting
    ;high_type help                - Show comprehensive help

  Revision History:
    v2.14.0 - 2026-08-12 - Configurable universal link color: setlinkcolor/clearlinkcolor commands,
                           per-frontend (link_default_color / link_default_color_gsl); all four
                           rendering sites derive from one cache; monsterbold excluded (bold too on GSL)
    v2.13.2 - 2026-08-12 - Fixed background-color bleed: \240 resets foreground only, so bg-setting
                           colors (thought, bg*, bgbright*) now end with \240+\221 (bg back to black);
                           bold-section strip pattern extended to cover palette bytes and resets
    v2.13.1 - 2026-08-12 - Renamed self.color to self.ht_color: trusted scripts share one binding and
                           htsorter's identically-named self.color was overwriting high_type's (last
                           load wins), sending literal XML preset tags to the Wizard instead of GSL bytes
    v2.13.0 - 2026-08-12 - GSL palette expansion from gsltest probe findings: thought (\222 white-on-blue)
                           and whisper (\213 bright cyan) now render on Wizard; added 30-name extended
                           Wizard palette (8 hues x normal/bright/bg/bgbright, GSL side only) assignable
                           via add/setcharcolor; new allcolors command shows standard set + palette grid
    v2.12.1 - 2026-08-12 - Multi-line output (showconfig, colors, help, debug) now emits as single
                           atomic blocks via respond/_respond array form - one header, no per-line
                           [high_type:] prefixes; color samples inline with their labels
    v2.12.0 - 2026-08-12 - Per-frontend configuration: XML side (types_to_color) and GSL side
                           (types_to_color_gsl) edited automatically per active FE; GSL side seeded
                           from XML defaults filtered to GSL-renderable colors; side-aware validation
                           and colors/showconfig; fixed [unknownscript] attribution on runtime
                           commands (hook thread has no Script.current - output now self-identifies)
    v2.11.0 - 2026-08-12 - Frontend awareness: GSL mode for Wizard/Avalon emits raw highlight bytes
                           (link/selectedlink -> \207, speech -> \212, bold -> GSL codes); colors with
                           no GSL equivalent (thought, whisper) are not applied; replaced dead
                           $fake_stormfront check with Frontend.supports_gsl?
                           (v2.6.0-v2.10.0 skipped - burned by the rolled-back NPC coloring line)
    v2.5.1 - 2026-08-12 - Fixed startup ordering crashes (reset/debug/first-run), version display drift,
                          color_all_links persistence; added color validation to add; deduplicated
                          startup/runtime code; fixed nested presets in character coloring; exact type matching
    v2.5.0 - 2025-09-20 - Added character default color feature (setcharcolor/clearcharcolor commands)
    v2.4.1 - 2025-09-20 - Internal refactoring
    v2.4.0 - 2025-09-20 - Added showconfig, remove commands and HT alias for runtime processing
    v2.3.0 - 2025-09-19 - Added runtime command processing for inline configuration
    v2.2.1 - 2025-09-18 - Fixed startup delay logic to only wait when session is recent (< 10 seconds)
    v2.2.0 - 2025-09-18 - Removed legacy maintenance commands (update, remove_styles) for cleaner code
    v2.1.1 - 2025-09-18 - Fixed version display consistency, removed duplicate bold color handling
    v2.1.0 - 2025-09-18 - Reduced defaults to 5 core types, fixed arg parsing, removed deprecated colors
    v2.0.3 - 2025-09-14 - Added help command with comprehensive usage information
    v2.0.2 - 2025-09-14 - Added remove_styles command to clean configuration (removed in v2.2.0)
    v2.0.1 - 2025-09-14 - Added 10-second startup delay for proper initialization timing
    v2.0.0 - 2025-09-14 - Added universal link coloring (replaces linktothefast functionality)
    v1.1.0 - 2025-09-14 - Removed redundant 'link' color assignments for magic items
    v1.0.0 - 2023-01-01 - Gift from Xanlin

          author: Ensayn
            game: GS
            tags: highlighting, colors, links, item_types
        required: Lich >= 4.6
         version: 2.14.0
=end
script.want_downstream_xml = true
script.want_downstream = false

# Single source of truth for version - interpolated into all version-bearing messages
@version = '2.14.0'
@script_name = script.name

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Frontend detection
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# GSL front-ends (Wizard/Avalon) cannot render XML preset tags - sf_to_wiz strips
# all tags before sending to the client. They render inline highlight bytes instead.
@gsl_mode = Frontend.supports_gsl?

@monsterbold_start = @gsl_mode ? "\034GSL\r\n " : "<pushBold\/>"
@monsterbold_end   = @gsl_mode ? "\034GSM\r\n " : "<popBold\/>"

# Standard color names (valid on both sides)
@valid_colors = %w[speech whisper thought link selectedlink bold monsterbold]

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Extended Wizard palette (GSL side only)
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Byte map discovered via the v2.12.2 gsltest probe: \201-\217 foreground colors
# (dark set then bright set), \220-\237 backgrounds (parallel structure, fg+\020),
# \240 reset. \207 (Links) and \212 (Speech) were the probe's confirmed controls.
# CAUTION: \240 resets the FOREGROUND only - background colors persist until the
# next bg code, so bg-setting colors must end with \240 + \221 (bg back to black).
@gsl_end = 0o240.chr
@gsl_bg_reset = 0o240.chr + 0o221.chr
@gsl_palette = {}
%w[black blue green cyan red magenta yellow white].each_with_index { |name, i|
  @gsl_palette[name]        = (0o201 + i).chr
  @gsl_palette["bg#{name}"] = (0o221 + i).chr
}
%w[blue green cyan red magenta yellow white].each_with_index { |name, i|
  @gsl_palette["bright#{name}"]   = (0o211 + i).chr
  @gsl_palette["bgbright#{name}"] = (0o231 + i).chr
}

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Output helper
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Runtime commands execute inside the UpstreamHook proc on Lich's client thread,
# where Script.current is nil - echo there prints [unknownscript: ...]. All output
# reachable from the hook path self-identifies via _respond instead.
def self.ht_echo(msg = '')
  _respond "[#{@script_name}: #{msg}]"
end

# Emit a multi-line report as ONE atomic block (respond/_respond accept arrays and
# send all lines in a single client write - no per-line prefixes, no interleaving).
# raw=true uses _respond so embedded color markup/bytes render instead of escaping.
def self.ht_block(lines, raw = false)
  raw ? _respond(lines) : respond(lines)
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# GSL color mapping (Wizard/Avalon)
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Returns [start_code, end_code] for colors the GSL protocol can render, or nil
# for colors with no GSL equivalent (per design: unmappable colors are NOT set).
# The highlight byte globals are populated by Lich core for the wizard FE.
def self.gsl_color_codes(color_type)
  name = color_type.to_s.downcase
  case name
  when "monsterbold", "bold"
    [@monsterbold_start, @monsterbold_end]
  when "link", "selectedlink", "selected"
    [$link_highlight_start.to_s, $link_highlight_end.to_s]
  when "speech"
    [$speech_highlight_start.to_s, $speech_highlight_end.to_s]
  when "whisper"
    [@gsl_palette['brightcyan'], @gsl_end]      # probe-confirmed \213 - Wizard Whispers look
  when "thought"
    [@gsl_palette['bgblue'], @gsl_bg_reset]     # probe-confirmed \222 - white on blue, Wizard Thoughts look
  else
    # Extended Wizard palette names (brightcyan, bgred, ...) - GSL side only
    return nil unless @gsl_palette.key?(name)
    # Background colors persist past \240 - end them with the bg-black reset too
    [@gsl_palette[name], name.start_with?('bg') ? @gsl_bg_reset : @gsl_end]
  end
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Per-frontend configuration sides
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# XML side: UserVars.types_to_color / character_default_color (shared with htsorter)
# GSL side: UserVars.types_to_color_gsl / character_default_color_gsl
# Commands automatically edit the side matching the active frontend.
def self.active_side
  @gsl_mode ? 'GSL' : 'XML'
end

def self.active_types
  @gsl_mode ? UserVars.types_to_color_gsl : UserVars.types_to_color
end

def self.set_active_types(hash)
  if @gsl_mode
    UserVars.types_to_color_gsl = hash
  else
    UserVars.types_to_color = hash
  end
end

def self.active_char_color
  @gsl_mode ? UserVars.character_default_color_gsl : UserVars.character_default_color
end

def self.set_active_char_color(color)
  if @gsl_mode
    UserVars.character_default_color_gsl = color
  else
    UserVars.character_default_color = color
  end
end

def self.active_link_color
  @gsl_mode ? UserVars.link_default_color_gsl : UserVars.link_default_color
end

def self.set_active_link_color(color)
  if @gsl_mode
    UserVars.link_default_color_gsl = color
  else
    UserVars.link_default_color = color
  end
end

# The universal link color appears in four rendering sites (XML phase 1 wrap,
# bold-exclusion strips, phase 2/3 wrapper-strip patterns, GSL fallback codes);
# all derive from this cache, recomputed at init and on setlinkcolor/clearlinkcolor
def self.refresh_link_color_cache
  lc = self.active_link_color
  preset_ids = { 'link' => 'link', 'speech' => 'speech', 'whisper' => 'whisper',
                 'thought' => 'thought', 'selectedlink' => 'selectedLink',
                 'selected' => 'selectedLink', 'bold' => 'bold' }
  @xml_link_open = "<preset id='#{preset_ids[lc] || 'link'}'>"
  codes = lc ? self.gsl_color_codes(lc) : nil
  @gsl_link_codes = codes || [$link_highlight_start.to_s, $link_highlight_end.to_s]
end

# Colors valid for the active side: standard names on both sides,
# plus the extended Wizard palette names on the GSL side only
def self.active_valid_colors
  @gsl_mode ? (@valid_colors + @gsl_palette.keys) : @valid_colors
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Color functions (unified from FSP)
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
def self.xml_encode(msg)
  return msg.encode(:xml => :text)
end

# Named ht_color (not color) - trusted scripts share one binding, and htsorter
# defines its own self.color; identical names overwrite each other, last load wins
def self.ht_color(msg, color_type, skip_encoding=false)
  # If msg already contains XML tags (like <a> tags), don't encode
  encoded_msg = skip_encoding || msg.include?('<a ') ? msg : self.xml_encode(msg)

  if @gsl_mode
    codes = self.gsl_color_codes(color_type)
    return encoded_msg if codes.nil? || codes[0].empty?
    return "#{codes[0]}#{encoded_msg}#{codes[1]}"
  end

  case color_type.downcase
  when "monsterbold"
    return "#{@monsterbold_start}#{encoded_msg}#{@monsterbold_end}"
  when "speech"
    return "<preset id=\"speech\">#{encoded_msg}</preset>"
  when "whisper"
    return "<preset id=\"whisper\">#{encoded_msg}</preset>"
  when "thought"
    return "<preset id=\"thought\">#{encoded_msg}</preset>"
  when "link"
    return "<preset id=\"link\">#{encoded_msg}</preset>"
  when "selectedlink", "selected"
    return "<preset id=\"selectedLink\">#{encoded_msg}</preset>"
  when "bold"
    return "<preset id=\"bold\">#{encoded_msg}</preset>"
  else
    self.ht_echo "Unknown color type: #{color_type}. Valid colors:"
    self.ht_echo "  #{@valid_colors.join(', ')}"
    return encoded_msg
  end
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Legacy helper functions (for compatibility)
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
def self.format_preset(msg, preset="speech")
  return self.ht_color(msg, preset)
end

def self.format_style(msg, style="roomName")
  return self.ht_color(msg, style)
end

def self.ts()
  return "#{Time.now.strftime('%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%S')}"
end

def self.sendto_familiar(msg, stamp=self.ts)
  _respond "<pushStream id=\"familiar\" ifClosedStyle=\"watching\"/>#{stamp};#{msg}\n<popStream/>\n"
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Configuration display and testing
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
def self.display_configuration
  lines = []
  lines << "=== High Type v#{@version} Configuration ==="
  lines << "Frontend: #{Frontend.client} (#{@gsl_mode ? 'GSL' : 'XML preset'} mode) - editing the #{self.active_side} config side"
  lines << ""
  lines << "Item types configured for highlighting (#{self.active_side} side): #{self.active_types.keys.size}"
  self.active_types.each { |type, color|
    if @gsl_mode && self.gsl_color_codes(color).nil?
      lines << "  #{type.ljust(12)} -> #{color} (no GSL equivalent - not applied)"
    else
      lines << "  #{type.ljust(12)} -> #{color}"
    end
  }
  lines << ""
  lines << "Universal link coloring: #{UserVars.color_all_links ? 'enabled' : 'disabled'} (shared across frontends)"
  lines << "  - Colors ALL links when enabled"
  lines << "  - Item types override with specific colors"
  lines << "  - Replaces linktothefast functionality"
  lines << "Universal link color (#{self.active_side} side): #{self.active_link_color || 'default (Links color)'}"
  if self.active_char_color
    lines << "Character default color (#{self.active_side} side): #{self.active_char_color}"
    lines << "  - All character names use this color instead of link default"
  else
    lines << "Character default color (#{self.active_side} side): not set (using link default)"
  end
  lines << ""
  lines << "Available colors (#{self.active_side} side): #{@valid_colors.join(', ')}"
  lines << "  plus #{@gsl_palette.size} extended palette names - see ;ht allcolors" if @gsl_mode
  lines << "Configuration stored in UserVars (XML side shared with other scripts)"
  lines << "=== End Configuration ==="
  self.ht_block(lines)
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Item type to color mapping configuration in UserVars for shared access
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
XML_DEFAULT_COLORS = {
  # Valuable items
  'gem'         => 'thought',      # Purple/magenta for gems
  'jewelry'     => 'thought',      # Same color family as gems
  'valuable'    => 'thought',      # Consistent with gems

  # Containers and boxes
  'box'         => 'speech',       # Speech color for lockboxes
  'boatcrate'   => 'whisper'       # Subdued for boat crates
} unless defined?(XML_DEFAULT_COLORS)

def self.setup_color_defaults
  # Initialize UserVars for both sides if not already set
  UserVars.types_to_color ||= {}
  UserVars.types_to_color_gsl ||= {}
  # ||= would clobber a persisted false, so only initialize when truly unset
  UserVars.color_all_links = true if UserVars.color_all_links.nil?

  # Seed XML side with standard defaults if empty
  if UserVars.types_to_color.empty?
    UserVars.types_to_color = XML_DEFAULT_COLORS.dup
    UserVars.save
  end

  # Seed GSL side with XML defaults filtered to GSL-renderable colors if empty
  if UserVars.types_to_color_gsl.empty?
    UserVars.types_to_color_gsl = XML_DEFAULT_COLORS.select { |_type, color| !self.gsl_color_codes(color).nil? }
    UserVars.save
  end
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Load only the type data we need for comparisons (active side)
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
def self.reload_type_data
  @high_type_data = GameObj.type_data.select { |k, _v| self.active_types.keys.include?(k) }
end

def self.identify_item_category(name,noun)
    list = @high_type_data.keys.find_all { |t| (name =~ @high_type_data[t][:name] or noun =~ @high_type_data[t][:noun]) and (@high_type_data[t][:exclude].nil? or name !~ @high_type_data[t][:exclude]) }
    return nil if list.empty?
    type = list.include?('collectible') ? 'collectible' : list.join(',');
    return type
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Shared command actions (used by both startup and runtime paths)
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
def self.show_color_examples
  sample_text = "Sample Item Text"
  lines = []
  lines << "=== High Type Color Examples (#{self.active_side} side - #{Frontend.client}) ==="
  lines << ""
  # Each active-side color rendered inline with its label
  %w[monsterbold speech whisper thought link selectedlink bold].each { |color_name|
    next unless self.active_valid_colors.include?(color_name)
    lines << "  #{(color_name + ':').ljust(14)} #{self.ht_color(sample_text, color_name)}"
  }
  lines << ""
  lines << "NOTE: If all colors look the same, your client presets may"
  lines << "      be configured to use the same 'skin' color for all presets."
  lines << "Extended palette: ;ht allcolors" if @gsl_mode
  lines << "=== End Color Examples ==="
  self.ht_block(lines, true)
end

def self.show_all_colors
  sample = "Sample"
  lines = []
  lines << "=== High Type All Colors (#{self.active_side} side - #{Frontend.client}) ==="
  lines << ""
  lines << "Standard colors (work on both frontends):"
  %w[monsterbold speech whisper thought link selectedlink bold].each { |color_name|
    lines << "  #{(color_name + ':').ljust(14)} #{self.ht_color(sample, color_name)}"
  }
  lines << ""
  if @gsl_mode
    lines << "Extended Wizard palette (GSL side only):"
    %w[black blue green cyan red magenta yellow white].each { |hue|
      row =  "  #{hue.ljust(8)} #{self.ht_color(sample, hue)}"
      row += "  bright: #{self.ht_color(sample, "bright#{hue}")}" if @gsl_palette.key?("bright#{hue}")
      row += "  bg: #{self.ht_color(sample, "bg#{hue}")}"
      row += "  bgbright: #{self.ht_color(sample, "bgbright#{hue}")}" if @gsl_palette.key?("bgbright#{hue}")
      lines << row
    }
    lines << ""
    lines << "Assign with: ;ht add <type> <name>   e.g. ;ht add gem brightcyan"
    lines << "NOTE: names follow the probe byte map - if a sample's color doesn't"
    lines << "      match its name, report it so the byte can be corrected."
  else
    lines << "Extended palette: available on Wizard/Avalon (GSL side) only."
  end
  lines << "=== End All Colors ==="
  self.ht_block(lines, true)
end

def self.add_type_color(type_arg, color_arg)
  type_name = type_arg.gsub(/["']/, '')  # Remove quotes if present
  color_name = color_arg.gsub(/["']/, '') # Remove quotes if present
  unless self.active_valid_colors.include?(color_name)
    self.ht_echo "Invalid color for the #{self.active_side} side: #{color_name}"
    self.ht_echo "Valid colors (#{self.active_side}): #{@valid_colors.join(', ')}#{@gsl_mode ? ' plus palette names (;ht allcolors)' : ''}"
    return false
  end
  self.active_types[type_name] = color_name
  UserVars.save
  self.reload_type_data
  self.ht_echo "Added (#{self.active_side} side): #{type_name} => #{color_name}"
  return true
end

def self.reset_config
  self.set_active_types({})
  self.setup_color_defaults
  self.reload_type_data
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# GSL colorization (Wizard/Avalon) - single pass
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Resolves each link's final color once (character color -> type color ->
# universal link fallback) and wraps it in highlight bytes. sf_to_wiz strips the
# <a>/<d> tags afterward, leaving the bytes around the plain text.
def self.apply_gsl_colors(game_output)
  begin
    return game_output unless game_output =~ /<[ad][ >]/

    link_codes = @gsl_link_codes

    colored = game_output.gsub(/<([ad])((?: [^>]*)?)>(.*?)<\/\1>/) do |whole_link|
      attrs = $2
      text  = $3
      codes = nil

      # Character names (negative exist IDs) use the character default color
      if self.active_char_color && attrs =~ /exist="-\d+"/
        codes = self.gsl_color_codes(self.active_char_color)
      elsif attrs =~ /exist="-?\d+" noun="([^"]+)"/
        # Item link: resolve type-specific color
        type = self.identify_item_category(text, $1)
        if type
          type_list = type.split(',')
          self.active_types.each { |k, v|
            if type_list.include?(k)
              codes = self.gsl_color_codes(v)
              break
            end
          }
        end
      end

      # No type/character color applied (or no GSL equivalent): universal link fallback
      codes = link_codes if codes.nil? && UserVars.color_all_links

      if codes.nil? || codes[0].empty?
        whole_link
      else
        "#{codes[0]}#{whole_link}#{codes[1]}"
      end
    end

    # Bold text exclusion: strip injected highlight bytes inside bold sections
    if @gsl_strip_pattern
      colored = colored.gsub(/<pushBold\s*\/>.*?<popBold\s*\/>/m) do |bold_content|
        bold_content.gsub(@gsl_strip_pattern, '')
      end
    end

    colored
  rescue
    # Encoding or matching failure: pass the line through uncolored
    game_output
  end
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Runtime command processing (using recolor.lic proven pattern)
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
def self.handle_runtime_command(args, running=true)
  return unless args

  # Parse the arguments if they come as a single string
  args = args.strip.split(/\s+/) if args.is_a?(String)
  return if args.empty?

  case args[0].downcase
  when "help"
    lines = []
    lines << "=== High Type v#{@version} Runtime Commands ==="
    lines << "Commands edit the #{self.active_side} config side (current frontend: #{Frontend.client})"
    lines << ""
    lines << "While script is running, use:"
    lines << "  ;high_type (or ;ht)         - Show current configuration"
    lines << "  ;high_type help (or ;ht help) - Show this help"
    lines << "  ;high_type add <type> <color> - Add/update type color"
    lines << "  ;high_type remove <type>     - Remove type color"
    lines << "  ;high_type showconfig        - Show current configuration"
    lines << "  ;high_type reset            - Reset #{self.active_side} side to defaults"
    lines << "  ;high_type colors           - Show standard color examples"
    lines << "  ;high_type allcolors        - Show standard + extended Wizard palette"
    lines << "  ;high_type setcharcolor <color> - Set default color for all characters"
    lines << "  ;high_type clearcharcolor  - Clear character color (use link default)"
    lines << "  ;high_type setlinkcolor <color> - Set universal link color"
    lines << "  ;high_type clearlinkcolor  - Clear link color (use default)"
    lines << ""
    lines << "Script continues running after commands."
    lines << "=== End Runtime Help ==="
    self.ht_block(lines)

  when "add"
    if args[1] && args[2]
      if self.add_type_color(args[1], args[2])
        self.ht_echo "Configuration updated (script continues running)"
      end
    else
      self.ht_echo "Usage: ;high_type add <type> <color>"
      self.ht_echo "Example: ;high_type add weapon speech"
    end

  when "reset"
    self.ht_echo "Resetting #{self.active_side} side configuration to defaults..."
    self.reset_config
    self.ht_echo "Configuration reset complete! (script continues running)"
    self.display_configuration

  when "colors", "examples"
    self.show_color_examples

  when "allcolors"
    self.show_all_colors

  when "showconfig", "config", "show"
    self.display_configuration

  when "remove"
    if args[1]
      type_name = args[1].gsub(/["']/, '')
      if self.active_types.key?(type_name)
        self.active_types.delete(type_name)
        UserVars.save
        self.ht_echo "Removed (#{self.active_side} side): #{type_name}"
        self.reload_type_data
        self.ht_echo "Configuration updated (script continues running)"
      else
        self.ht_echo "Type '#{type_name}' not found in the #{self.active_side} side configuration"
      end
    else
      self.ht_echo "Usage: ;high_type remove <type>"
      self.ht_echo "Example: ;high_type remove weapon"
    end

  when "setcharcolor"
    if args[1]
      color_name = args[1].gsub(/["']/, '')
      if self.active_valid_colors.include?(color_name)
        self.set_active_char_color(color_name)
        UserVars.save
        self.ht_echo "Character default color (#{self.active_side} side) set to: #{color_name}"
        self.ht_echo "All character names will now use #{color_name} color"
      else
        self.ht_echo "Invalid color for the #{self.active_side} side: #{color_name}"
        self.ht_echo "Valid colors (#{self.active_side}): #{@valid_colors.join(', ')}#{@gsl_mode ? ' plus palette names (;ht allcolors)' : ''}"
      end
    else
      self.ht_echo "Usage: ;high_type setcharcolor <color>"
      self.ht_echo "Example: ;high_type setcharcolor whisper"
    end

  when "clearcharcolor"
    self.set_active_char_color(nil)
    UserVars.save
    self.ht_echo "Character default color (#{self.active_side} side) cleared - characters will use link default"

  when "setlinkcolor"
    if args[1]
      color_name = args[1].gsub(/["']/, '')
      excluded = @gsl_mode ? %w[bold monsterbold] : %w[monsterbold]
      if self.active_valid_colors.include?(color_name) && !excluded.include?(color_name)
        self.set_active_link_color(color_name)
        UserVars.save
        self.refresh_link_color_cache
        self.ht_echo "Universal link color (#{self.active_side} side) set to: #{color_name}"
        self.ht_echo "All links now use #{color_name} unless a type color overrides them"
      else
        self.ht_echo "Invalid link color for the #{self.active_side} side: #{color_name}"
        self.ht_echo "Valid: #{(@valid_colors - excluded).join(', ')}#{@gsl_mode ? ' plus palette names (;ht allcolors)' : ''}"
      end
    else
      self.ht_echo "Usage: ;high_type setlinkcolor <color>"
      self.ht_echo "Example: ;high_type setlinkcolor brightcyan"
    end

  when "clearlinkcolor"
    self.set_active_link_color(nil)
    UserVars.save
    self.refresh_link_color_cache
    self.ht_echo "Universal link color (#{self.active_side} side) cleared - using the default link color"

  else
    # Default to showing configuration
    self.display_configuration
  end
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Initialize configuration BEFORE argument handling so every startup path
# (reset, debug, add, first run) has methods and type data available
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
self.setup_color_defaults
self.reload_type_data
self.refresh_link_color_cache

# Precompute the byte-strip pattern for bold-section exclusion in GSL mode
# (the highlight byte globals are populated by Lich core before scripts start).
# Includes the extended palette bytes and resets - any injected code must strip.
@gsl_strip_pattern = nil
if @gsl_mode
  strip_codes = ([$link_highlight_start, $speech_highlight_start,
                  $link_highlight_end, $speech_highlight_end, @gsl_end] +
                 @gsl_palette.values).map(&:to_s).reject(&:empty?).uniq
  @gsl_strip_pattern = Regexp.union(strip_codes) unless strip_codes.empty?
end

# Handle initial startup arguments - parse manually since Lich may pass as single string
if script.vars[0]
  # Split the arguments manually if they come as a single string
  args = script.vars[0].split(/\s+/)

  case args[0].downcase
  when "quiet"
    echo "High Type loaded silently - #{self.active_types.keys.size} item types configured (#{self.active_side} side)"
  when "reset"
    echo "Resetting #{self.active_side} side configuration to defaults..."
    self.reset_config
    echo "Configuration reset complete!"
    self.display_configuration
    exit
  when "add"
    if args[1] && args[2]
      if self.add_type_color(args[1], args[2])
        self.display_configuration
      end
    else
      echo "Usage: ;high_type add <type> <color>"
      echo "Example: ;high_type add boatcrate whisper"
    end
    exit
  when "debug"
    lines = []
    lines << "=== High Type v#{@version} Debug Info ==="
    lines << "Frontend: #{Frontend.client} (#{@gsl_mode ? 'GSL' : 'XML preset'} mode) - #{self.active_side} config side"
    lines << "Configured types (#{self.active_side}): #{self.active_types.keys.join(', ')}"
    lines << ""
    lines << "GameObj type data loaded for:"
    @high_type_data.each { |type, data|
      lines << "  #{type}: name=#{data[:name].inspect}, noun=#{data[:noun].inspect}"
    }
    lines << ""
    lines << "Testing 'salvage crate' items:"
    test_names = ["a cheap salvage crate", "a shoddy salvage crate", "a silver salvage crate"]
    test_names.each { |name|
      type = self.identify_item_category(name, "crate")
      lines << "  '#{name}' => type: #{type || 'nil (no match)'}"
    }
    lines << "=== End Debug ==="
    self.ht_block(lines)
    exit
  when "colors", "examples"
    self.show_color_examples
    exit
  when "allcolors"
    self.show_all_colors
    exit
  when "help"
    lines = []
    lines << "=== High Type v#{@version} Help ==="
    lines << ""
    lines << "USAGE: ;high_type [command]"
    lines << ""
    lines << "PER-FRONTEND CONFIG:"
    lines << "  Commands edit the config side matching your frontend:"
    lines << "  - Wrayth/Stormfront -> XML side (all 7 colors)"
    lines << "  - Wizard/Avalon     -> GSL side (speech, link, selectedlink, bold, monsterbold)"
    lines << "  Current: #{Frontend.client} -> #{self.active_side} side"
    lines << ""
    lines << "STARTUP COMMANDS:"
    lines << "  quiet             Load silently with item count (script keeps running)"
    lines << "  reset             Reset active side to defaults (exits)"
    lines << "  add <type> <color> Add or update type color (exits)"
    lines << "  colors            Show standard color examples (exits)"
    lines << "  allcolors         Show standard + extended Wizard palette (exits)"
    lines << "  debug             Show debug information and test cases (exits)"
    lines << "  help              Show this help message (exits)"
    lines << ""
    lines << "RUNTIME COMMANDS (script continues running):"
    lines << "  ;high_type        Show current configuration"
    lines << "  ;high_type help   Show runtime command help"
    lines << "  ;high_type add <type> <color> Add or update type color"
    lines << "  ;high_type remove <type>     Remove type color"
    lines << "  ;high_type showconfig        Show current configuration"
    lines << "  ;high_type reset  Reset active side to defaults"
    lines << "  ;high_type colors Show standard color examples"
    lines << "  ;high_type allcolors Show standard + extended Wizard palette"
    lines << "  ;high_type setcharcolor <color> Set default color for all characters"
    lines << "  ;high_type clearcharcolor    Clear character color (use link default)"
    lines << "  ;high_type setlinkcolor <color> Set universal link color"
    lines << "  ;high_type clearlinkcolor    Clear link color (use default)"
    lines << ""
    lines << "FEATURES:"
    lines << "  - Frontend-aware: XML presets on Wrayth/Stormfront, GSL codes on Wizard/Avalon"
    lines << "  - Per-frontend configuration (XML and GSL sides edited independently)"
    lines << "  - Runtime command processing for dynamic configuration"
    lines << "  - Universal link coloring (replaces linktothefast)"
    lines << "  - Item type-specific highlighting using GameObj data"
    lines << "  - XML-side configuration shared with other scripts via UserVars"
    lines << ""
    lines << "EXAMPLES:"
    lines << "  ;high_type add gem thought      # Gems use purple color (XML side)"
    lines << "  ;high_type add gem speech       # Gems use speech color (works both sides)"
    lines << "  ;high_type colors               # Show color examples for this frontend"
    lines << "=== End Help ==="
    self.ht_block(lines)
    exit
  else
    echo "Unknown startup command: #{args[0]}"
    echo "Startup commands: quiet, reset, add, colors, debug, help"
    echo "For runtime commands (remove, showconfig, setcharcolor, ...), start the script first."
    exit
  end
else
  self.display_configuration
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# hook proc
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
@match_patterns = Hash.new
@match_patterns[:item_link] = /<a exist="(?<id>-?\d+)" noun="(?<noun>[^"]+)">(?<name>[^<]+)<\/a>/;

# Main processing pipeline for game output colorization
# GSL front-ends: single-pass byte colorization; XML front-ends: 3-phase preset tagging
apply_type_colors = proc {|game_output|
  if @gsl_mode
    game_output = self.apply_gsl_colors(game_output)
  else
    # Phase 1: Universal link enhancement - Apply base coloring to all link elements
    # (wrap tag comes from the link-color cache so setlinkcolor is honored)
    if UserVars.color_all_links && game_output =~ /<[ad](?: [^>]*)?>.*?<\/[ad]>/
      game_output = game_output.gsub(/(<[ad](?: [^>]*)?>.*?<\/[ad]>)/, "#{@xml_link_open}\\1</preset>")

      # Bold text exclusion: Remove link coloring from bold sections to prevent conflicts
      game_output = game_output.gsub(/<pushBold\s*\/>.*?<popBold\s*\/>/) do |bold_content|
        bold_content.gsub(/#{Regexp.escape(@xml_link_open)}(.*?)<\/preset>/, "\\1")
      end

      # Additional bold tag handling for compatibility
      game_output = game_output.gsub(/<b\s*>.*?<\/b\s*>/) do |bold_content|
        bold_content.gsub(/#{Regexp.escape(@xml_link_open)}(.*?)<\/preset>/, "\\1")
      end
    end

    # Phase 2: Character default color - Apply color to all character names (negative exist IDs)
    # Strips any Phase 1 link-preset wrapper first to avoid nested presets
    if self.active_char_color && game_output =~ /<[ad] exist="-\d+"/
      game_output = game_output.gsub(/(?:#{Regexp.escape(@xml_link_open)})?(<([ad]) exist="-\d+"[^>]*>[^<]+<\/\2>)(?:<\/preset>)?/) do
        "<preset id='#{self.active_char_color}'>#{$1}</preset>"
      end
    end

    # Phase 3: Type-specific colorization - Override colors based on GameObj classification
    if game_output =~ /<a exist="(?:-?\d+)" noun="(?:[^"]+)">(?:[^<]+)<\/a>/
      color_queue = []
      game_output.scan(@match_patterns[:item_link]).each { |id,noun,name|
        type = self.identify_item_category(name,noun)
        next if type.nil?
        type_list = type.split(',')
        self.active_types.each { |k,v|
          if type_list.include?(k)
            color_queue << [id,v]
            break
          end
        }
      }
      if color_queue.size > 0
        color_queue.each { |id,color_type|
          # Remove any existing preset wrapper and apply type-specific color
          item_pattern = /(#{Regexp.escape(@xml_link_open)})?(<a exist="#{id}".*?<\/a>)(<\/preset>)?/
          game_output.gsub!(item_pattern, self.ht_color('\\2', color_type, true))
        }
      end
    end
  end

  game_output
}

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# Startup delay to ensure proper initialization before other scripts depend on it
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
startup_delay = ((Time.now - $login_time) < 10 ? (10 - (Time.now - $login_time)).ceil : 0)
if startup_delay > 0
  echo "High Type v#{@version} starting - waiting #{startup_delay} seconds for session stabilization..."
  sleep startup_delay
else
  echo "High Type v#{@version} starting - session already stable, no delay needed..."
end

#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
# hook it (using recolor.lic proven pattern)
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------#
runtime_pattern = /^(?:<c>)?\s*#{Regexp.escape($lich_char)}(?:#{Regexp.escape(script.name)}|ht)(\s+.*)?$/

DownstreamHook.add('high_type', apply_type_colors)
UpstreamHook.add('high_type_commands', proc { |cmd|
  if cmd =~ runtime_pattern
    if $1
      self.handle_runtime_command($1, true)
    else
      _respond "[#{script.name} is already running. Type ;#{script.name} help for runtime commands.]"
    end
    nil  # Prevent command from going to game
  else
    cmd  # Pass other commands through
  end
})

before_dying{
  DownstreamHook.remove('high_type')
  UpstreamHook.remove('high_type_commands')
}

echo "High Type v#{@version} fully active - #{@gsl_mode ? 'GSL highlight codes' : 'link coloring and type highlighting'} enabled (#{Frontend.client}, #{self.active_side} config side)"
echo "Runtime commands available: ;high_type (or ;ht) help, ;high_type add <type> <color>, ;high_type reset, etc."

while true;sleep 1;end
